            "Correct screening-eligibility decisions by condition: Jev 99.1%, 99.9%, 94.4%; Haiku 97.8%, 98.4%, 98.1%; Sonnet 100.0%, 99.6%, 99.8%; Luna 99.7%, 98.8%, 98.5%; Sol 100.0%, 99.8%, 99.6%. On the complex condition, \"Jev produced 27 false positive and 14 false negative screening flags per 1,000 notes\", the most of any system.",
            "Reported cost per 1,000 notes spans a factor of more than thirty: Luna $0.12–$0.21, Jev $0.61–$0.64, Sol $2.44–$4.22, Haiku $3.37–$4.43, Sonnet $3.76–$6.61 — the kind of figure that decides whether a screening tool runs on every note or none.",
